==English==

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|en|la|abiūdicātus}}, perfect passive participle of {{m|la|abiūdicō||deprive or take away by judicial sentence}}, from {{m|la|ab||from, away from}} + {{m|la|iūdicō||pass judgement; determine, conclude}}. {{doublet|en|abjudge}}. See [[judge]].

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|legal}} To reject by judicial sentence.
# To [[abjudge]].

